  </div>
</div>

<p>In addition to these documents, a <strong>100% Declared‑Value Marine Transit Insurance</strong> is highly recommended. This type of insurance guarantees that the bike’s full market value is covered in the event of loss, damage, or theft during marine transit. The policy should specify:</p>

<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>The exact declared value of the bike.</span></li>
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Coverage limits that match or exceed the bike’s market worth.</span></li>
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Clear clauses for marine perils, including collision, fire, and piracy.</span></li>
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Exclusions and conditions that might affect claim settlement.</span></li>
</ul>

<p>Having a 100% declared‑value policy not only protects the owner’s investment but also satisfies the stringent requirements of many shipping lines and customs authorities. It demonstrates due diligence and mitigates potential financial exposure arising from unforeseen incidents during the voyage.</p>

<p>Before the bike departs, double‑check that each document is legible, signed, and stamped where necessary. Keep both original and photocopy copies, and retain electronic backups in a secure cloud storage. Proper documentation expedites customs clearance, reduces delays, and ensures compliance with the regulatory framework governing bike transportation in Daund and beyond.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


