      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Destination Handover, Odometer Sign-Off &amp; Joint Condition Inspection for Bike Transportation In Daund</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>When a two‑wheeler or motorcycle arrives at the destination, the handover process is designed to preserve the integrity of the vehicle and the accuracy of the transport record. The first step is a daylight re‑inspection, which compares the current condition of the bike with the photographs taken at the pickup point.</p>
<p>This visual audit checks for new dents, scratches, or fluid leaks that might have arisen during transit. The inspector records any discrepancies on a digital log and, if necessary, captures fresh photos to document the issue before it becomes a claim point.</p>

<p>Next, the odometer reading is verified against the original LR bilty. The bilty lists the mileage at departure, and the destination rider must read the odometer and confirm the figure matches or falls within the acceptable variance window.</p>
<p>A mismatch triggers a brief investigation: the rider explains any sudden mileage changes, and the dispatcher cross‑checks the GPS telemetry that accompanied the shipment. The odometer confirmation is entered into the same log as the visual inspection, ensuring a single, auditable trail of the vehicle’s condition and usage.</p>

<p>Once the visual and mileage checks are complete, the final handover step is the signed condition sign‑off. The destination rider signs a digital or paper form that confirms the vehicle’s condition at handover and acknowledges receipt of the bike in the same state as documented.</p>
<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">The signature is time‑stamped and stored in the transport management system, creating an immutable record that can be referenced in the event of a dispute.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>If any damage or mileage issue is noted, the rider must also sign a note explaining the circumstances, and the transport manager must approve the claim before the handover is considered final.</span></li></ul>

